    <fullDescription>
      <Value Culture="en-US"><![CDATA[<p ><strong>Department: Sales &amp; Business Development<br>Reports to: SDR/BDR Team Lead<br>Employment Type: Full-Time</strong></p>

<p >Job Summary:</p>

<p >The Business Development Representative (BDR) is responsible for prospecting and qualifying leads, focusing on larger healthcare organizations, multi-location practices, and high-volume clinics. The BDR engages with decision-makers, nurtures relationships, and sets up high-value demo meetings for Sales Executives. The role requires strategic outreach, persistence, and a consultative approach to drive opportunities forward.</p>

<p >Key Responsibilities:</p>

<p >Lead Generation &amp; Qualification</p>

<ul >
<li>Work with assigned leads from the dialer/CRM while also generating new leads online (LinkedIn, social media, healthcare databases, and industry networks).</li>

<li>Target larger organizations, including hospital groups, multi-location practices, and high-volume clinics.</li>

<li>Identify and engage with key decision-makers (C-suite executives, Physicians Owner, practice administrators, or senior medical staff).</li>

<li>Conduct thorough research on target organizations to personalize outreach.</li>

<li>Communicate the value of RPM &amp; CCM in a compelling and tailored manner.</li>
</ul>

<p >Sales Engagement &amp; Demo Scheduling</p>

<ul >
<li>Schedule high-value demo meetings for Sales Executives.</li>

<li>Build relationships through multi-touch outreach (calls, emails, LinkedIn messaging).</li>

<li>Manage complex sales cycles, ensuring long-term engagement with potential clients.</li>

<li>Overcome objections and address key concerns to maintain prospect interest.</li>
</ul>

<p >Pipeline Management &amp; Performance Targets</p>

<ul >
<li>Achieve a minimum of 10 attended demos per month.</li>

<li>Maintain accurate and up-to-date CRM records for all interactions.</li>

<li>Collaborate closely with Sales Executives to ensure a smooth handoff and proper follow-up.</li>
</ul>

<p >Qualifications &amp; Requirements:</p>

<ul >
<li>2+ years of experience in B2B sales, business development, or lead generation (preferably in healthcare or SaaS).</li>

<li>Proven ability to engage with senior decision-makers and navigate complex sales cycles.</li>

<li>Strong research, communication, and consultative selling skills.</li>

<li>Experience using CRM systems, LinkedIn Sales Navigator, and other prospective tools.</li>

<li>Self-driven, highly organized, and able to manage a large pipeline of leads.</li>
</ul>]]></Value>
    </fullDescription>
    <jobTitle>
      <Value Culture="en-US"><![CDATA[BD Representative]]></Value>
    </jobTitle>
    <shortDescription>
      <Value Culture="en-US"><![CDATA[Centro is seeking a motivated and strategic Business Development Representative (BDR) to join our Sales & Business Development team. Reporting to the SDR/BDR Team Lead, you will play a key role in generating and qualifying leads within the healthcare sector, targeting larger organizations and high-volume practices. The ideal candidate has a proven track record in B2B outreach, excels in building relationships with senior decision-makers, and is driven to meet and exceed monthly performance targets.]]></Value>
    </shortDescription>
